  "checks": [
    "Positive stdin/stderr terminal detection, stdout detection with and without redirection, and Handle/Stream.isTty on /dev/tty.",
    "A concurrent Lean timer produces its marker before the external driver sends any input to the blocked reader.",
    "Raw Unicode/CRLF line bytes followed by binary input and all 256 stdout byte values survive without decoding or line transformation.",
    "The driver measures a full 4096-byte stdout pipe before notifying Lean over stdin; Lean verifies its 16384-byte writer task is unfinished while the pipe remains unread.",
    "Only the Lean confirmation releases the reader; all output bytes and normal task completion then match both native oracles.",
    "Driver controls retain child failures, enforce deadlines/output bounds, and reject a marker-only claim of a full pipe."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Linux x64 only; other operating systems/architectures remain unverified.",
    "Raw terminals only: canonical input, terminal resizing and job control are separate coverage gaps.",
    "These supplementary cases do not prove all console, file, scheduler or standard API behavior."
  ],
